   "summary": "Author: CreativeTools\r\n3DBenchy is a 3D model specifically designed for testing and benchmarking 3D printers.",
   "description": "<h3>Update: <a href=\"https://www.nti-group.com/home/information/news/3dbenchy/\">The Iconic 3DBenchy Enters the Public Domain</a></h3><p><br><br>Author: CreativeTools</p><p>3DBenchy is a 3D model specifically designed for testing and benchmarking 3D printers. It is a small recognizable object that you can download for free, make and share.</p><p><a href=\"http://www.3dbenchy.com/\">http://www.3dbenchy.com/</a></p><h3>Print instructions</h3><p>Maybe you have seen on some prints the infamous Benchy hull line. We eliminated that in our presliced gcode. Check the article, how we did that.<br><a href=\"https://help.prusa3d.com/en/article/the-benchy-hull-line_124745\">The Benchy hull line</a></p>",
